{
"from": 115,
"to": 142,
"text": "- **Not run: mutation.** No `run --mutants` (`inputs#I1` item 4). Each guard's strength is its one-shot control   (below); a control mutates source, so it is no entry. - **Not run: live legs.** No live `claude` start (`inputs#I1` item 3; `inputs#I2` item 2, PROVISIONAL). The claim is   that viola counts the array the CLI sends; that the 2.1.325 CLI fills it is read-from-source and carried to   «Standing live rig with a screen model». Live starts asked: 0. - **No smoke.** No boot-path touchpoint: the start path, the plugin files and the snapshot are untouched; the booted   cases boot their wrapper themselves. - **Why CI is read.** The operator pass pushes the chunk's tree and reads its run on CI's one leg, `ubuntu-latest`   (G2 and G4 read the booted case's home there). No OS-conditional site is added. - **Thresholds.** The chunk adds no numeric threshold. The booted cases' waits are WITHIN = 12 s, below the mutants   profile's 15 s kill and cargo-mutants' 20 s floor `(test-plan · bootstrap-phases-derive-for-route-setup-project/decision/mutants-kill-below-cargo-mutants-timeout)`;   each control's `--timeout` sits above its filtered entry's own run time. - **Controls, each one-shot through `gate.py control`** (gate-contract §Control), each on an entry filtered to the   guard's own cases, its cases by name (the last token of the nextest line, read from implement's first run):   - `wake-count` — `--timeout 300` on entry 5; guard: the length in `data_of`'s Stop arm (written `null`); cases the     `empty`, `two` and `not_objects` rows of `turn_ended_scheduled_wakes_counts_the_session_crons_array`.   - `wake-drift` — `--timeout 300` on entry 5; guard: `session_crons` in `known_fields`' `\"array\"` arm (the word     then reads `\"string\"`); cases the `string`, `object` and `number` rows of     `turn_ended_scheduled_wakes_is_null_when_absent_or_not_an_array`.   - `wake-key` — `--timeout 300` on entry 9; guard: `\"scheduled_wakes\"` in TurnEnded's `data_keys`; case     `state_events_scheduled_wakes_is_a_known_key` (the reader then counts it unknown).   - `wake-content` — `--timeout 600` on entry 10; forces the behaviour on (an absence case): `Known.session_crons`     typed `Option<serde_json::Value>` and the Stop arm writing it whole; case     `hook_a_stop_holding_scheduled_wakes_carries_their_count_and_no_content`.   The wake rule's case (step 6) and the MCP case (step 11) pin pass-through behaviour that has no guard to remove: the   wake reads no data key and the handler copies the `ok` payload; they carry no control. The exact `old`/`new` texts   are written by /implement against its own diff; «holds» = the named cases ran and FAILED with no TIMEOUT line   (`inputs#I1` item 4). Control ids stay within 16 characters."
}
],
